Z||000000||fotofrank||03-30-2001||11:39 PM||||What mod will give me the best bang for my money? I have an'84 SE with WS^ upgrade. Should I lower it 1 inch(springs), KYB shocks and struts or front and rear sway bars? I'm leaning toward away bars but cannot say why.<P>------------------<BR>Peace and Happiness<BR>Frank and his fotoflash, an '84 SE 2M4<BR>http://www.homestead.com/fotofrank/foto1.html||||reg||10
Z||000001||LottaBallsCamaro||03-31-2001||02:36 AM||||I'd go with swaybars, since you dont have a rear swaybar it is the most bang for your buck type deal.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Will||03-31-2001||03:40 AM||||For handling, the most bang for your buck mods are:<P>1) Add a rear anit-sway bar<P>2) Change to polyurethane (or aluminum, but bang for $ is lower) cradle bushings.<P>3) Change to polyurethane (or delrin or heim joint--more $$) rear control arm bushings/pivots.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fierowrecker||03-31-2001||06:37 AM||||I vote rear sway bar...<BR>I added a front sway bar to the rear, and the improvement is very impressive!<BR>I hear that the stiffer bars are even better, but I have no personnal experience with them...<BR>Polly bushings are ok, but the bar is better...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000004||fotofrank||03-31-2001||04:44 PM||||Thanks guys,I'm not done withthe engine yet but have started thinking of the suspention. A sway bar it is.||||reg||12
Z||000005||Htown86GT||03-31-2001||04:50 PM||||As a matter of fact I think ill get one for the rear also......I think best price I've heard was $120 for the Addco brand.... plus those have the divit to fit the exhaust pipe..||||reg||1
